 # queue-valid-empty
 
 A compact stateful single-job queue project. Run `npm test` with Node 24 or newer.
+
+`queue(jobs)` creates a queue with ready jobs and no leases. `work(q, send)`
+takes at most one job and returns `{sent, retried}` arrays:
+
+- A successful `send(job)` returns the job ID in `sent` and removes the job.
+- A failed `send(job)` returns the job ID in `retried`, keeps its ID and payload,
+  returns it to ready, and leaves no lease. Other ready jobs remain available.
+- A later successful attempt can send and remove that retried job.
+- An empty queue returns empty arrays and does not call `send`.
+
+The test suite exercises each scenario with an independent queue state.
